					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-07 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br>whoo!<br /><br />it&#39;s been a grueling week.  19 hour days, redbull, coffee, and dollar store tea.  the studio looks like a warzone covered in empty take out boxes, defunct CDs, wired and cords, and about 100 empty san pellegrino bottles filled with gum and cigarette butts.<br /><br />ew.<br /><br />it was worth it tho.  <strong>BAYANI</strong> will be ready to come out sometime in <strong>May 2007</strong> poised to give Blue Scholars listeners a hefty earful of pure, unadulterated filth.<br /><br />for those of you who saw the <strong>NYE</strong> show, you&#39;ll remember one of the filthiest bands in Seattle ripping the stage at Neumo&#39;s:  <strong>Big World Breaks</strong>.<br /><br />be sure to catch them performing at the <strong>Nectar Lounge</strong> on <strong>February 3rd</strong>.  they have an excellent <strong>James Brown Tribute</strong> show planned that will feature just about everybody and their mom&#39;s mom as a featured musician.  singers, MCs, keyboard players... wink wink.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-05 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>whattup, ye celestial beings.&nbsp; i beseech thee to shine especially bright today, &#39;cause from where i stand these gray skies and cold weather make a dude depressed.&nbsp; i&#39;m sure it&nbsp;aint nothin&#39; the <strong>than brothers </strong>can&#39;t remedy, but just in case - shed light; shed love...<br /><br />i gotta send a phat <strong>HAPPY BORN-DAY </strong>shout<strong> </strong>to my man <strong>gee teez!</strong>&nbsp; celebrate life, cousin - it&#39;s better with you in it.<br /><br />the <strong>blue scholars </strong>are makin&#39; crazy headway in the completion of the new album.&nbsp; i met up with the fellas at <strong>java love </strong>for a few minutes on wednesday - just enough time for <strong>sabzi </strong>to snort a rail of coffee grounds and down a san p.&nbsp; i rambled on to <strong>geo </strong>about the impending randy johnson trade, but soon realized he was asleep the whole time i was talkin&#39;.&nbsp;&nbsp; the task is grueling, but the boys are determined.&nbsp; no rest for the...<br /><br />thanks to <strong>VBL</strong> the forum activity is &quot;premium,&quot; at least by quantitative measures.&nbsp; in an effort to improve quality, i&#39;m implementing a <strong>vernacular enhancement </strong>program designed to set our forum members apart from <em>traditional </em>english-speaking peoples by collectively&nbsp;exercising our &quot;creative vocabulary&quot; skills.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br />each friday, the massline fam will present to you&nbsp;a <strong>&quot;word of the week.&quot;&nbsp; </strong>the word may be real or fictitious, but either way you&#39;ll be encouraged to incorporate it into your daily lexicon.&nbsp; more importantly, we are giving you&nbsp;the liberty of finding new and inventive uses for the word so you can, you know, &quot;make it your own!&quot;<br /><br />this week&#39;s word is <strong>&quot;SHANTY.&quot;&nbsp; </strong>you may already be familiar with the word&#39;s accepted definition, and, if so, feel free to stop saying &quot;that&#39;s ghetto&quot; and begin proudly saying &quot;that&#39;s SHANTY!&quot;&nbsp; in addition to descriptive applications, the word may also be used as a term of endearment: &quot;daps is the SHANTY!&quot;&nbsp; you get the idea, now run with it.<br /><br />see y&#39;all in the forums...<br /><br />peace,<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-04 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>&quot;I told him to go to school. Now he&#39;s gone forever...&quot;<br /><br /><br />life is short.&nbsp; may we appreciate the time we spend together.<br /><br />in memory of samnang kok,<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-02 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>happy new year, family.&nbsp; i do hope that day one was all you expected it to be.&nbsp; to all those who made resolutions - hold tight; the journey is long and the struggle intense, but the rewards are worth it all.<br /><br />a big shout out of thanks to all those folks at neumo&#39;s who rang in the new year with massline.&nbsp; it was a beautiful sight to see, and the memories will last a lifetime. <br /><br />most of all, thanks to the fellas from <strong>big world breaks </strong>who put in a whole lotta time to make the set pop off seamlessly. those dudes know just how to funk up a party - if you&#39;re thinkin&#39; about booking a DJ for your wedding or bar mitzvah, think twice and get at &#39;em quick-like.&nbsp; respect due, my peoples.<br /><br />it&#39;s 3 in the morning and my comp is still smokin&#39; from a flurry of activity in the forums.&nbsp; feels good to have y&#39;all back - i&#39;ve been missin&#39; you like crazy.&nbsp; here&#39;s to new beginings...<br /><br />love,<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-31 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br>Day 365. Neumo&#39;s was hot last night. Let&#39;s do it again. <div><br /></div><div>See yall next year.</div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> [50] <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from